Here’s what was wrong and how it’s fixed:

| Problem | Why it fails | Fix |
|---------|--------------|-----|
| `document.getAnimations("t3")` | There is no method called `getAnimations`. You meant **getElementById**. | Use `document.getElementById('t3')`. |
| Variables `num1`, `num2`, `num3` | They don’t exist – you already declared `n1`, `n2`, `n3`. | Replace every occurrence of `num*` with `n*`. |
| Missing `parseFloat()` / conversion to a number | Inputs are read as strings (`"5"` vs `5`). Comparing `"10" > "2"` works lexicographically, not numerically. | Convert each value with `Number()` or `parseFloat()`. |
| Semicolons & extra spaces in `getElementById` calls | Spaces inside the parentheses break the syntax. | Write `document.getElementById('id')` without spaces. |
| Logic for “largest” is incomplete | Only one branch compares `n2 > n3`. It never checks whether `n2` is larger than `n1` or `n3`. | Compare each candidate against both others (using `>=` so equal numbers still pick the right one). |

---

### Corrected HTML + JavaScript

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>Largest Number</title>
</head>
<body>

<p>Write a program to find the largest number among 3 numbers.</p>

<input type="text" placeholder="Enter 1st number" id="t1">
<br>
<input type="text" placeholder="Enter 2nd number" id="t2">
<br>
<input type="text" placeholder="Enter 3rd number" id="t3">
<button onclick="check()">Check</button>
<h3 id="ans">The largest number is</h3>

<script>
    function check(){
        // Grab the input elements
        let t1El   = document.getElementById('t1');
        let t2El   = document.getElementById('t2');
        let t3El   = document.getElementById('t3');

        // Read and turn them into numbers (handles leading/trailing spaces)
        let n1 = parseFloat(t1El.value);
        let n2 = parseFloat(t2El.value);
        let n3 = parseFloat(t3El.value);

        // Make sure at least one of them is a valid number
        if (isNaN(n1) || isNaN(n2) || isNaN(n3)) {
            document.getElementById('ans').innerHTML = "Please enter valid numbers.";
            return;
        }

        // Find the maximum
        if (n1 >= n2 && n1 >= n3) {
            document.getElementById('ans').innerHTML =
                "The largest number is " + n1;
        } else if (n2 >= n1 && n2 >= n3) {
            document.getElementById('ans').innerHTML =
                "The largest number is " + n2;
        } else {
            document.getElementById('ans').innerHTML =
                "The largest number is " + n3;
        }
    }
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

**What changed?**

* `document.getElementById('t1')` etc. – removed stray spaces.
* Added `parseFloat(...)` to convert the text input to a proper number.
* Replaced `getAnimations` with `getElementById`.
* Used consistent variable names (`n1`, `n2`, `n3`).
* Compared each value against *both* others (`>=`) so the logic covers all three possibilities.
* Added a quick check for non‑numeric input and gave a friendly message.

Now clicking **Check** will display the correct largest number.

